From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: ICorDebug over Wine Mono's soft debugger agent -- processes and threads

NET-DBG phase 2 (first part). Wine Mono has no CLR debugging services; its
debugger agent speaks Mono's soft debugger protocol (SDB). ICorDebug is now
its client, over the user's own socket (sgdbgsock.dll, 7791):
- CreateProcess gives the debuggee the agent (dt_unix, server, suspended)
  in its environment; the first Continue starts it and connects to the
  agent as it comes (given up when the process goes or is released).
- DebugActiveProcess attaches to a program running its agent (server,
  not suspended), stopped, with the CreateProcess callback; a program
  without one: CORDBG_E_DEBUGGING_NOT_POSSIBLE.
- Stop and Continue count as documented and suspend and resume the
  managed threads (VM SUSPEND/RESUME); Detach lets the program run on
  (VM DISPOSE); Terminate closes the connection.
- EnumerateThreads and GetThread (stopped only; else
  CORDBG_E_PROCESS_NOT_SYNCHRONIZED): ICorDebugThread with the OS thread id,
  handle, process, debug state and user state (the thread's ThreadState);
  stacks, values, stepping and evaluation are not there yet.
sdb.c: the SDB connection -- handshake, protocol version, requests and
their replies matched by a reader thread.
---
